MT7932 host protocol and lifecycle regression tests
=================================================

Run with Python 3 and a host C compiler (no Apple hardware needed):

    for test in tools/testing/selftests/mt7932/test_*.py; do
        python "$test" || exit
    done

These tests compile the actual driver parsers/callbacks with host mocks and
ASan/UBSan. They were moved into the kernel series from the cleanroom enablement
repository so that a kernel-only checkout retains the self-contained coverage.
They do not prove DMA coherency, RF behavior or physical device operation.

Additional own-device calibration, stock configuration and regulatory fixture
tests remain in linux-enablement-mac-alpha/tests; they require its extraction
tools and local opaque firmware inputs. Those fixtures are not redistributed.
